{"kind":"article","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Equatable Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/Equatable-Implementations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)"],"title":"Operators","anchor":"Operators","generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct\/equatable-implementations"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct/!=(_:_:)":{"abstract":[],"title":"!=(_:_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"!=","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Tied","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-tied indicates the presence of a tie within a metric relationship mark. As with the tied"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element, both the start and stop of the tie should be specified, in this case within separate metronome-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome.Note","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol"}}}